WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.301
There's one really cool thing about our apartment.

2
00:00:17.302 --> 00:00:20.829
Well, actually, there are two really cool things.

3
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:26.221
The first cool thing is my bedroom, where I do most of my inventing.

4
00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:29.409
The second cool thing is our fireplace.

5
00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.006
Most apartment buildings don't have fireplaces.

6
00:00:33.007 --> 00:00:38.909
But our building is really old, and there are lots of fireplaces.

7
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.282
We have one in our living room.

8
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:50.552
Shortly after Tate stopped yelling at me for taking the last granola bar, my mom came home from work.

9
00:00:50.553 --> 00:00:52.522
It was raining outside.

10
00:00:52.523 --> 00:00:58.051
Thunder boomed and lightning flashed.

11
00:00:58.052 --> 00:01:02.592
"This is a good night to make a fire," my mom said.

12
00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:06.815
So after dinner my mom built a fire in the fireplace.

13
00:01:06.816 --> 00:01:10.021
Molly, Josh, and Jenny came over.

14
00:01:10.022 --> 00:01:13.729
We all sat on the rug in front of the crackling fire.

15
00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:19.565
We played cards while the rain beat against the windows.

16
00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:22.256
Soon Molly fell asleep.

17
00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:26.897
She still wasn't getting much sleep because of bad dreams about monsters.

18
00:01:26.898 --> 00:01:36.794
We let Molly sleep and played cards without her.

19
00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:42.042
I was getting sleepy myself when I heard the wail of a fire engine.

20
00:01:42.043 --> 00:01:46.995
Then came the sound of a smoke detector in our building.

21
00:01:46.996 --> 00:01:48.820
Molly woke up suddenly.

22
00:01:48.821 --> 00:01:51.899
"Is the apartment on fire?" she cried.

23
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:57.396
"No," my mom said. "Everything is fine here."

24
00:01:57.397 --> 00:02:01.095
I glanced at the fire in our fireplace.

25
00:02:01.096 --> 00:02:03.973
The fire was almost out.

26
00:02:03.974 --> 00:02:09.145
But the sound of the siren was really close now.

27
00:02:09.146 --> 00:02:13.961
I ran to our front windows and looked out.

28
00:02:13.962 --> 00:02:18.247
"The fire truck stopped in front of our building!" I cried.

29
00:02:18.248 --> 00:02:21.084
"And the firefighters are jumping out!"

30
00:02:21.085 --> 00:02:23.545
My mom looked alarmed.

31
00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:27.679
"Uh-oh. We'd better get out of the building fast!" she said.

32
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.969
Most of the people who lived in our building were already standing outside on the sidewalk.

33
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:37.907
Mr. Chen was there, and Molly's mom and dad were there with Caswell.

34
00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:42.661
They rushed over and gave Molly a hug.

35
00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:46.025
"I called the fire department," said Molly's dad.

36
00:02:46.026 --> 00:02:48.945
"Our TV exploded!"

37
00:02:48.946 --> 00:02:51.601
Most little kids would be scared.

38
00:02:51.602 --> 00:02:53.106
But not Caswell!

39
00:02:53.107 --> 00:02:57.155
Instead he was grinning and looking pretty excited.

40
00:02:57.156 --> 00:03:02.799
"There was a big bang and lots of smoke!"

41
00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.449
We watched the firefighters enter the buidling.

42
00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.961
They were wearing special helmets and carrying long hoses.

43
00:03:10.962 --> 00:03:14.032
Soon they came outside again.

44
00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:17.204
One was carrying Molly's TV.

45
00:03:17.205 --> 00:03:22.001
"Everything is fine," the firefighter told Molly's parents.

46
00:03:22.002 --> 00:03:26.405
"Except for your TV," added another firefighter.

47
00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:29.362
"I guess you'll need to buy a new one."

48
00:03:29.363 --> 00:03:36.164
"Maybe one of the monsters from Monster Madness made it explode," said Caswell.

49
00:03:36.165 --> 00:03:39.220
The first firefighter laughed.

50
00:03:39.221 --> 00:03:43.764
"I don't think that was the reason," he said.

51
00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:47.349
"The fire was probably caused by the lightning."

52
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:51.769
"Thank goodness we're all safe!" said Mrs. O'Donnell.

53
00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.428
I noticed that Molly didn't look sleepy anymore.

54
00:03:55.429 --> 00:03:56.910
She looked happy.

55
00:03:56.911 --> 00:04:01.838
Just before we all went back inside, she leaned over to me.

56
00:04:01.839 --> 00:04:04.541
"Iggy," she whispered.

57
00:04:04.542 --> 00:04:08.243
"This is the best thing that ever happened!"

58
00:04:08.244 --> 00:04:12.829
"The fire truck coming to our building?" I said in surprise.

59
00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:18.601
"No," said Molly. "My family's TV exploding."

60
00:04:18.602 --> 00:04:25.735
She grinned. "No more watching Monster Madness after school every day!"

61
00:04:25.736 --> 00:04:33.705
I nodded. I hadn't invented anything to solve Molly's problem, but it had solved itself.

62
00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:37.782
Molly didn't have to worry about scary monster shows anymore.

63
00:04:37.783 --> 00:04:42.965
Molly's parents left the TV sitting out on the curb.

64
00:04:42.966 --> 00:04:48.312
"Good-bye, TV!" said Molly happily.

65
00:04:48.313 --> 00:04:51.753
There was one thing she didn't expect though.

66
00:04:51.754 --> 00:04:58.279
Her mom and dad bought another TV the next day!

67
00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:03.107
So Caswell and Lucy went back to watching Monster Madness.

68
00:05:03.108 --> 00:05:09.262
And poor Molly went back to not sleeping.
